# Everything this build pins. Included by the Makefile; override any of it on the command line.

# --- kernel ------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The talos-kernel release whose signed kernel and amneziawg module this installer ships. Its
# version is the Talos release it was built for, vX.Y.Z+sm.N, and the installer and the
# extensions take that Talos release from it, so they cannot name a different one. Bump it after
# a talos-kernel release.
KERNEL_RELEASE=v1.14.5+sm.1

# The amneziawg module's version, for the amneziawg extension's manifest. `make check-pins`
# compares it with the AWG_REF that KERNEL_RELEASE was built from.
AWG_REF=v3.1.20260906

# --- daemons -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# ghcr.io/slipmesh/talos-extensions, by digest: the awg, router and nftables daemons and their
# extension-service specs. A `sha-<commit>` tag from talos-extensions' main or a release tag of
# it; the digest is what the build pulls, the tag only says where it came from.
DAEMONS_IMAGE=ghcr.io/slipmesh/talos-extensions:sha-cf60d651f9df0ae7b3dc29315ce5ebe945de7021@sha256:ca4c6e6d2205b34b3464f6e84f64b5dc80bf382542d8bfd268270c450034f4d0

# --- nftables ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# siderolabs/pkgs, as the `git describe` string Talos publishes for its release; nftables-pkg is
# built in a checkout of it. `make check-pins` compares it with the one KERNEL_RELEASE's Talos
# release was built from.
PKGS=v1.14.0-48-gf4bda77

# netfilter.org's libmnl -> libnftnl -> nftables, built statically from source by
# pkgs/nftables-pkg. Each is upstream's latest stable release, independent of the versions
# siderolabs/pkgs builds; regenerate the hashes with `make hashes` after changing a version.
LIBMNL_VERSION=1.0.5
LIBMNL_SHA256=274b9b919ef3152bfb3da3a13c950dd60d6e2bcd54230ffeca298d03b40d0525
LIBMNL_SHA512=16fa48e74c9da7724a85c655dfb0abd8369392627934639d65de951543e1447ac3e048d231248f1ce8861443c2ef62654a85a81feeedbbffaf2e5744f6cf4c9f

LIBNFTNL_VERSION=1.3.2
LIBNFTNL_SHA256=c97abc3409f8fa396b4462b2bb7f147a3a47a4ddc97cfa0b2f18890c9cfde8b0
LIBNFTNL_SHA512=ee60231f25c51ce45a8117e5a255265964ed024184c6b5ff4a883e6bbab6b0a66a73b6ca31be1c7055d778c5e7d780f483437eb9d27028dd9fcb6cc69af676ca

# kube-proxy's bundled nft below 1.0.6.1 crashes on the set-element userdata format nft >= 1.1.3
# writes (kubernetes/kubernetes#136786, fixed by #140405, in v1.36.3). Kubernetes >= 1.36.3 is
# therefore required alongside this nft.
NFTABLES_VERSION=1.1.7
NFTABLES_SHA256=a6fbf060d8d4fff001517a2b94f356bb4366bfbf0ba366366f9d27cc38caa58f
NFTABLES_SHA512=4dc900ad6e74c4ce532df974287bd3d5382ccabcee9e61b7639071abae70c215a8dea04d1f5af6f0f431e5717bd98db12dc858b00b51f284a17b488ef648b73d

# nft links musl statically from the tools image PKGS selects, and musl's MIT license asks for its
# notice to travel with the binary. This tarball is fetched for that COPYRIGHT file only, so it has
# to name the musl that image carries; nftables-pkg's test fails when the two differ.
MUSL_VERSION=1.2.6
MUSL_SHA256=d585fd3b613c66151fc3249e8ed44f77020cb5e6c1e635a616d3f9f82460512a
MUSL_SHA512=1adad96eddb3a2eb0cacb3e363b0046568925fcdd75cf8b0503f2139df1f693d64730779ca0ce8131b7624ab2d37f4247bb1d3393c523de6e30d2b1d7732555c

# --- router ------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Upstream tags, built unmodified by the router-bird and router-bird-exporter stages. BIRD is cloned
# from github.com/CZ-NIC/bird, upstream's own mirror: gitlab.nic.cz throttles unauthenticated
# requests and refuses GitHub Actions' address range. A tag can be moved, so the build also checks
# out exactly BIRD_COMMIT, the commit BIRD_REV names; the exporter needs no such pin, the Go
# checksum database already verifies it.
BIRD_REV=v3.4.0
BIRD_COMMIT=c3669497e3949b942d86d07e343092cc439b4659
BIRD_EXPORTER_REV=v1.7.1

# --- where the images go -----------------------------------------------------------
# Extensions as $(REGISTRY)/<name>, nftables-pkg as $(REGISTRY)/nftables-pkg, the installer as
# $(REGISTRY)/talos-installer. CI builds against a registry local to the job (see `make publish`).
REGISTRY=ghcr.io/slipmesh
